		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: My Baofeng 1701 keeps rebooting without letting me use it]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4724&amp;p=34974#p34974"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello, yesterday I received my Baofeng 1701 and as a good amateur I installed OpenGD77. After that everything went well and I kept configuring the radio but I changed an option that made the radio turn off. I looked for key combinations until I reset it with the buttons. After that, I don't know what happened to the radio but it started to turn off and on without resetting itself each time and asking me for the language, I tried to configure it and the radio restarted again. This has continued since yesterday. I have tried everything, but nothing has worked for me. Is there anyone out there who knows the solution?<br><br>Video: <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ea1XcWz_63bifSckUDPTRuRvt6ZnymXM/view?usp=sharing" class="postlink">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ea1XcW ... sp=sharing</a></div></blockquote>Start the radio in safe boot mode, then flash a fresh and clean codeplug.<br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#boot-key-combinations" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... mbinations</a><br><br>Also, you can also erase the voice prompts (using the CPS, Extras -&gt; OpenGD77 support menu), and upload a fresh list of DMR ID (Extras -&gt; Download callsign database)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Dec 31, 2024 3:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
